notes={
'home':('home.hero1','The split hero reads naturally as 手元のデータから / Anki カードを生成. Actions distinguish generating a deck, inspecting examples and reviewing updates; the AI request stays local. Read every business and framework catalog value, including copy-failure recovery and the intentional machine Optional literal.',(5,5,5,5)),
'examples':('examples.intro','The introduction tells readers to read source, flip cards and import downloads. ノート1件 versus カード1枚 remains distinct, the one-note/two-version change is explicit, and the Anki settings/local-edit limitation is adjacent to the update demonstration.',(5,5,5,5)),
'blog':('blog.heading','カード作成の実践と設計 replaces the English pun with a useful Japanese heading. Article category labels, RSS wording, read-link labels and navigation remain coherent with both translated historical articles.',(5,5,5,5)),
'docs':('Anki Forge は、ノート','The entry page separates notes, templates, cards and decks before giving a language/task route. Section headings are concise actions in a consistent register; the four guide groups and contribution pointers preserve the source task structure.',(5,5,5,5)),
'languages':('Rust、Node / TypeScript、Python','The selection table keeps programming languages distinct from content languages. Native optional dependencies and ordinary CPython/wheel prerequisites are placed immediately below installation choices; no Anki installation is implied.',(5,5,5,5)),
'quickstart':('Rust 1.92 以降','The short prerequisite/install/save/run/import sequence is readable. Spanish and hola/hello remain example content, while 名前空間 and 安定キー explain durable identity without promising client review-state preservation.',(5,5,5,5)),
'json-to-anki':('JSON にある生物学','Read the entire three-language recipe against English: shared inputs, exact filenames, three notes/three cards/two media and the first-answer-only update are retained. Client import limitations and the original-distribution baseline are explicit. Technical loanwords such as optional dependency remain understandable in context.',(5,4,4,5)),
'csv-to-anki':('Python と Anki Forge','The CSV guide clearly assigns parsing to Python and package generation to Anki Forge. Quoting/BOM, unique stable IDs, non-existing output destination and three-note/card import checks are separate actionable instructions; classifiers match their objects.',(5,5,5,5)),
'ai-anki-cards':('AI アシスタントに学習メモ','The corrected introduction states that Anki Forge is the library responsible for card generation. The workflow distinguishes drafting from source verification and export; PDF/OCR, local prompt assembly and the no-ID-regeneration condition remain explicit.',(5,5,5,5)),
'anki-forge-vs-genanki':('繰り返し公開する手順','The comparison offers a balanced keep-or-migrate decision, correctly acknowledges genanki identity support and distinguishes current SDKs from historical Rust-only measurements. Native-dependency and review-history caveats remain readable.',(5,4,5,5)),
'development':('このガイドはリポジトリ','The opening identifies source checkout and unreleased work before giving toolchain instructions. Native/facade tarballs and source wrappers are kept distinct from registry packages; commands and version names stay literal.',(5,4,5,5)),
'rust-guide':('1つの `Project`','Owned models/media, observation-only reports, atomic addition and stable source keys remain distinct. The revised 機能別モジュール wording avoids a public-domain licensing reading. Tool recipe v2, rejected v1 and ankiforge-identity-v1 are not confused with public package version 0.3.1.',(5,4,5,5)),
 'templates':('ノートタイプのテンプレート','The full bundle workflow explains immutable models, key references, explicit assets and source-directory independence. UTF-8 bytes versus schema character counts and per-file limits remain differentiated; the imperative steps are easy to follow despite technical density.',(5,4,5,5)),
'api':('Anki Forge は Rust コア','The task-to-SDK matrix gives recognizable Japanese action labels and preserves the note/media/diagnostics/update distinctions. The baseline paragraph explicitly rejects an Anki re-export as a substitute for complete original evidence.',(5,5,5,5)),
'installation':('Rust 1.92 以降','Public crate installation and JSON parser dependencies are stated separately; feature gating and host prerequisites are near the affected step. The final guide list names concrete next tasks without inventing a generic converter.',(5,5,5,5)),
'concepts':('`Project` は','The concept sequence connects Project, note, model, fields, cards and deck destinations. Text versus explicit HTML, retained media dependencies and artifact-owner lifetime remain distinct; update policy is not presented as a client-history guarantee.',(5,4,5,5)),
'cards':('Anki で1枚ずつ','ノート2件 and カード3枚 correctly express note/card cardinality; Basic front/back and Cloze deletion numbers are distinct. Reserved back_extra, Text/HTML behavior and identity changes when renumbering clozes are explained next to the relevant action.',(5,5,5,5)),
'custom-notetypes':('モデルを一度完成','The immutable-model/key/display-name distinction is consistent throughout. Reread the final key-validation clarification: 空白だけ and 前後に空白 precisely qualify the problematic keys rather than banning every internal space. Required/sort/generation rules remain readable.',(5,5,5,5)),
'media':('発音音声付き','The prose separates externally created media, immutable import snapshots, explicit raw-HTML assets and export naming. The repaired 拒否時のバイト数 uses the right measurement noun. MIME renaming, independent build inspection and process/pool budgets retain their limits.',(5,4,5,5)),
'image-occlusion':('プログラムから Anki','The caller-supplied rectangle requirement, no label detection, EXIF-oriented finite coordinates, one card per mask and ordinal reservation are explicit. The opening repeats setup and loosely calls a note importable; later steps correctly identify the APKG, so a minor wording issue remains.',(5,4,5,4)),
'updates':('すでに配布した Anki','The complete comparison/policy/client workflow preserves original distribution APKG, category-wide allowances, non-allowable hard failures, no deletion synchronization and no blanket review-history promise. Prepared publication is described as the same inspected candidate, not a second build.',(5,4,5,5)),
'build-guarantees':('`Project::build` は','Read the final copy-source correction together with the next persist_to sentence: the existing handle keeps its source while each new destination is resolved at that call. Native paths, unpaired UTF-16, late durability errors and consuming prepared owners are distinct.',(5,4,5,5)),
'troubleshooting':('失敗した操作','Symptoms and remedies align in each table. Image Occlusion is spelled out rather than ambiguous IO; addition atomicity, policy rejection versus operation failure and temporary-file ownership give actionable recovery instructions.',(5,5,5,5)),
'compatibility':('2026-10-13','Verification dates and counts remain historical evidence, with supported package availability separated from every-host guarantees. Unverified runtimes, codecs and client import settings are explicit, and the Japanese names for execution environments are consistent.',(5,4,5,5)),
'rust-api':('よく使う値は','The reference preserves API identifiers while explaining owned values, finite inspection counters, report/output distinction and lossless path representations. 機能別モジュール and 対になっていない clarify two revised phrases. 深く凍結 remains a minor calque in the shared addition-context paragraph.',(5,4,5,4)),
'node-quickstart':('Node.js 22.13','The Node version/native dependency prerequisite, .mjs save/run steps and persistent artifact behavior are direct. ESM/CommonJS/TypeScript links retain their roles; Japanese instructions distinguish the file remaining on disk from closing the handle.',(5,5,5,5)),
'node-api':('`ankiforge` エントリーポイント','Read all tables and prose: asynchronous workers, snapshot timing, relative-path anchoring, report property casing and consumed prepared owners remain separate. The image builder is named explicitly at .build(). Deep freezing has an understandable but unnatural literal Japanese phrase, recorded as minor.',(5,4,5,4)),
'python-quickstart':('仮想環境を作成','The venv/Windows activation, supported wheel, save/run/import and next-task sequence uses consistent concise Japanese. Stable namespace/note key and no-Anki export condition remain explicit.',(5,5,5,5)),
'python-api':('この SDK は','The revised 成功・失敗という処理結果 removes an unnecessary ordinary English noun. The sample corrections explicitly identify image-builder .build() and Create policy configuration errors; value ownership, GIL/fork handling and consumed publication owners remain readable.',(5,4,5,5)),
'python-diagnostics':('ビルドに成功すると','The final 公開 API の各種例外 and 対になっていない wording is natural and precise. Comparison completion differs from a blocked policy, budget increases are deliberate, and publication stage plus source-handle survival guide recovery.',(5,4,5,5)),
'python-migration':('`python -m pip install','The table contrasts old and new API shapes without suggesting alias compatibility. Package/import spellings, explicit stable keys, ordinary Text and original-package baseline conditions retain their distinctions.',(5,5,5,5)),
'genanki-migration':('ライブラリを選んでいる','The migration table maps concepts rather than claiming object emulation. Durable business IDs, explicit HTML/media dependencies and separately validated identity mapping are explained before the deliberate identity boundary.',(5,4,5,5)),
'blog:your-first-anki-deck':('学習内容がスクリプト','The tutorial flows naturally from one Spanish greeting to code, installation, stable identity and further examples. Historical date/category stay intact and the actual expanded Rust source is unchanged; current-installation links avoid silently upgrading the article narrative.',(5,5,5,5)),
'blog:stable-ids-and-deck-updates':('生成したデッキが','The hello→hello; hi table makes content versus identity concrete. Original distribution package, separate baseline/output paths and client-local-state caveats remain explicit, without promising lossless import behavior.',(5,5,5,5))
}
